# Known Archon bugs (not stylistic Postgres differences) — these entries
# assert that Archon *keeps* diverging from correct behavior. If a bug is ever
# fixed, its test should move to supported/ rather than being silently updated
# in place, so the fix is visible in the diff. See ddl.slt (in supported/) for
# the corpus format convention, including the note on `DbError`'s Debug format
# for `statement error` patterns.
#
# Per Slice-1 spec, these are real bugs in the engine, not gaps — do not
# attempt them against real Postgres (the out-archon-pgcompat oracle crate
# skips divergent/ entirely; see its own doc comment).
#
# Fact #2 (a qualifier naming a table not in the join silently fell back to
# matching by trailing segment, instead of erroring) was fixed: qualified
# names whose qualifier names no in-scope table now error via
# `executor::find_value`. Its regression test moved to
# supported/join_qualified_column.slt.
